<div class="activity-toolbar no-print">
    <a href="/ks3/year7/unit2.html" class="action-btn">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i>
        Unit 2
    </a>

    <button type="button" class="action-btn" data-export-pdf>
        <i class="fa-solid fa-file-arrow-down"></i>
        Export to PDF
    </button>

    <a href="john-doe.html" class="action-btn action-btn--primary">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-folder-open"></i>
        Open dossier
    </a>
</div>

<div class="unit-details">
    <div class="content-box">
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-bolt"></i> Quick Start</h2>

        <div class="quick-look-grid">
            <div class="quick-look-item">
                <span class="quick-look-kicker"><i class="fa-solid fa-stopwatch"></i> Time</span>
                <p>20–30 minutes</p>
            </div>
            <div class="quick-look-item">
                <span class="quick-look-kicker"><i class="fa-solid fa-list"></i> You need</span>
                <p>Exercise book, a pen, and the John Doe evidence dossier.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="quick-look-item">
                <span class="quick-look-kicker"><i class="fa-solid fa-inbox"></i> Hand in</span>
                <p>A completed investigation table and your reflection.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-2-col">
        <div class="content-box step-card">
            <span class="step-pill">Step 1</span>
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-user-secret"></i> Open the John Doe Dossier</h2>

            <p>You will explore a set of images from a fictional person called John Doe. All of these images were found publicly online.</p>

            <ul class="checklist">
                <li>Open the dossier and scan all 15 evidence images.</li>
                <li>For each image, ask: “What does this reveal about John?”</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="activity-toolbar no-print" style="margin: 1rem 0 0; justify-content: flex-start;">
                <a href="john-doe.html" class="action-btn action-btn--primary">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-folder-open"></i>
                    Open dossier
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="content-box step-card">
            <span class="step-pill">Step 2</span>
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-table"></i> Set Up Your Investigation Table</h2>
            <p>Create this table in your exercise book (one row per evidence image):</p>

            <div class="table-scroll">
                <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 0.95rem;">
                    <thead>
                        <tr style="background: #f8f9fa; border-bottom: 2px solid #e0e0e0;">
                            <th style="padding: 10px; text-align: left; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;">Image number</th>
                            <th style="padding: 10px; text-align: left; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;">What does this image reveal?</th>
                            <th style="padding: 10px; text-align: left; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;">Public or private? Why?</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0; color: #888;">(e.g. 1)</td>
                            <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;"></td>
                            <td style="padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;"></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <p>Fill in the table as you look at the images. Choose any details you spot, big or small.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box step-card">
        <span class="step-pill">Step 3</span>
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i> Find 10+ Clues</h2>

        <p>Using the evidence images, find at least <strong>10 pieces of information</strong> about John.</p>
        <p>Your list must include:</p>
        <ul class="custom-list">
            <li>John’s name</li>
            <li>John’s date of birth (day + month)</li>
            <li>The city John lives in</li>
        </ul>
        <p>After that, add any other clues you can reasonably work out (hobbies, routine, places he visits, things he likes, family information, etc.).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-2-col">
        <div class="content-box step-card">
            <span class="step-pill">Step 4</span>
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-lock"></i> Decide: Public or Private?</h2>

            <p>In the last column of your table, explain whether each clue should be public or private.</p>
            <ul class="checklist">
                <li>Could this help someone identify or locate John?</li>
                <li>Could this harm John’s reputation or safety?</li>
                <li>Is it “nice to share” or “risky to share”?</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="content-box step-card">
            <span class="step-pill">Step 5</span>
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-pen-to-square"></i> Reflection</h2>

            <div class="callout">
                <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>A.</strong> What picture can you build of John Doe?</h3>
                <p>Write 4–5 bullet points describing what kind of person John appears to be based only on the information you found.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="callout">
                <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>B.</strong> What should have stayed private?</h3>
                <p>Choose three items from your table that you think should not have been shared publicly. For each one, write one sentence explaining the risk or concern.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box step-card">
        <span class="step-pill">Step 6</span>
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-comments"></i> Partner Discussion</h2>
        <p>Discuss your findings with the person next to you. Share one thing you discovered that you didn’t expect.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-graduation-cap"></i> By the end of this task, you should be able to…</h2>
        <ul class="custom-list" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
            <li>Explain the difference between public and private information online</li>
            <li>Recognise how small pieces of data can build a picture of someone</li>
            <li>Understand why sharing too much online can be risky</li>
            <li>Describe what responsible digital behaviour looks like</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>
